{%- comment -%}
  Plaay - renders a fils amount exactly the way fmtAED() in assets/plaay-cart-tier-bar.js
  does: "AED 175", or "AED 0.01" when there are stray fils.

  The shop's money format is "{{amount}} AED", so the `money` filter renders "175.00 AED" -
  different word order AND different decimals from the client renderer. Server-rendered
  copy would visibly reformat the instant the JS took over after a cart change. This keeps
  the two twins byte-identical.

  Usage: {%- render 'plaay-aed', fils: remaining_fils -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign aed_whole = fils | divided_by: 100
  assign aed_frac = fils | modulo: 100
-%}
{%- if aed_frac == 0 -%}AED {{ aed_whole }}
{%- elsif aed_frac < 10 -%}AED {{ aed_whole }}.0{{ aed_frac }}
{%- else -%}AED {{ aed_whole }}.{{ aed_frac }}
{%- endif -%}
